196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (Prior literature investigates whether task-specific small language models \(SLMs\) can match general-purpose large language models \(LLMs\) at a fraction of energy and emissions. While small models perform competitively on structured classification tasks, complex reasoning and generative tasks often present distinct trade-offs. Furthermore, many published emission figures rely on theoretical estimates scaled from aggregate data rather than direct hardware measurements. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
